(4. Vector Indexing: FAISS IndexFlatL2 vs. HNSW) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 674 Td
13 TL
(Facebook AI Similarity Search \(FAISS\) provides highly optimized vector operations for) Tj
T* (GPU and CPU architectures. The IndexFlatL2 index performs exhaustive exact Euclidean) Tj
T* (distance search with zero recall loss, making it optimal for datasets with fewer than) Tj
T* (50,000 vectors. For web-scale vector search exceeding millions of embeddings,) Tj
T* (Hierarchical Navigable Small World \(HNSW\) graphs offer logarithmic search complexity) Tj
T* (O\(log N\) by traversing multi-layer proximity graphs with approximate nearest neighbor) Tj
T* (\(ANN\) guarantees.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
0.1 0.2 0.4 rg
50 561 Td
(5. Retrieval Top-K and Similarity Thresholds) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 545 Td
13 TL
(Standard RAG configurations query the vector database for the top-k most similar) Tj
T* (passages \(typically k=3 to k=6\). When cosine similarity falls below a critical) Tj
T* (threshold \(e.g., 0.45 or distance > 1.10\), the chunks are discarded to prevent context) Tj
T* (pollution. Context pollution occurs when irrelevant or noisy text confuses the) Tj
T* (attention mechanism of the generator LLM, leading to degraded synthesis quality.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
0.1 0.2 0.4 rg
50 458 Td
